    "title":  "StrategyPackage manifest schema still binds platform runtime policies instead of alpha core only",
    "description":  "Expected: StrategyPackage frozen manifest should bind only factor/model alpha core: factor set/order/schema, model spec/weights/training evidence, source lineage, and artifact hashes. Daily strategy, portfolio top_k, universe/ST PIT, minute execution, tail handling, risk/event/HMM, broker, account, and approval state should live in platform runtime profile, validated execution policy, release/binding version, or activation records. Old docs must be superseded by docs/architecture/strategy_package_platform_boundary_contract_20260520.md.\nActual: backend/services/strategy_package/models.py still requires strategy_config, universe_policy, portfolio_policy, execution_policy, minute_execution_policy, and risk_policy in StrategyPackageManifest. backend/services/strategy_package/qe_source_resolver.py still copies QE custom_params, stock_pool, topk/n_drop, execution/backtest frequency, and minute_execution_policy into the frozen manifest. This keeps platform runtime decisions inside the StrategyPackage boundary and causes later Selection/Paper/MiniQMT paths to treat package metadata as executable runtime authority.",
